# haikuporter-cmake-policy-minimum.patch  (issues #47 and #136)
#
# Patches haikuporter, not a recipe. Applied on the native arm64 builder by
# graviton/scripts/haiku-provision-native-builder (anchored, idempotent, verified)
# right after the haikuporter clone -- the native builder clones upstream
# haikuporter fresh, so a committed edit-in-place is how this fix reaches it (the
# same shape as haiku-haikuporter-patch does for the retired QEMU-guest fleet).
#
# TWO edits, two layers -- see "THE GENERAL FIX" (#47, cmakeDirArgs) and "THE
# SYSTEMIC FIX" (#136, filteredEnvironment) below. The second is the one that
# reaches every cmake invocation; the first is kept as belt-and-braces.
#
# WHY
# ---
# CMake 4.x removed the compatibility shim for `cmake_minimum_required(VERSION
# <3.5)`. Any port -- or a bundled third-party tree inside one -- that still
# declares an old minimum fails at configure time, at CMakeLists.txt before it
# looks at anything else. This is a recurring class, not a one-off:
#   * openal-1.21.1        (fixed per-recipe: -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5)
#   * libjxl-0.6.1         (bundled third_party/sjpeg needs it; per-recipe today)
#   * json_c-0.15          (json_c-0.15-cmake4-policy.patch, per-recipe)
# and every future CMake port carrying an old minimum will hit it again.
#
# THE GENERAL FIX
# ---------------
# CMake 4.0 added the `CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM` cache variable, which raises
# the *floor* of the compatibility policy version to the given value while leaving
# projects that request a newer minimum untouched -- so `=3.5` is a safe blanket
# default. A host environment variable is NOT a usable channel here:
# HaikuPorter/Utils.py:filteredEnvironment() passes only LC_ALL, TERM,
# LIBRARY_PATH and PATH into the build shell, so anything exported on the box is
# stripped before BUILD() runs.
#
# The channel that DOES reach every recipe is haikuporter's own `cmakeDirArgs`
# shell variable (HaikuPorter/Port.py). It is the shared string every CMake recipe
# already passes to `cmake` (openal and libjxl both use `$cmakeDirArgs`). Appending
# the policy flag there applies it to every CMake port at once -- and, because it
# is a cache variable, it propagates to add_subdirectory()'d bundled trees
# (libjxl's sjpeg, its highway) with no per-bundle handling. Recipes that still
# carry an explicit -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 keep working (a duplicate
# -D of the same value is harmless).
#
# THE EDIT (HaikuPorter/Port.py, the cmakeDirArgs assignment):
#
#   		self.shellVariables['cmakeDirArgs'] \
#   			= ' '.join('-DCMAKE_INSTALL_%s=%s' % (k, v)
#   				for k, v in cmakeDirArgs.items())
# +			# graviton/DeBeOS (#47): default every CMake port's floor policy to
# +			# 3.5 so cmake 4.x still configures projects/bundled trees that
# +			# declare cmake_minimum_required(<3.5). Cache var, so it reaches
# +			# add_subdirectory() bundles too; projects asking for more are
# +			# unaffected.
# +			self.shellVariables['cmakeDirArgs'] += ' -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5'
#
# THE LIMIT OF THE cmakeDirArgs CHANNEL (why #136 exists)
# -------------------------------------------------------
# The cmakeDirArgs edit above only helps recipes that actually PASS $cmakeDirArgs
# to cmake. Most CMake recipes hand-write an explicit `cmake -D... <src>` argument
# list and never reference $cmakeDirArgs -- so the flag never reaches them. That
# is exactly why the #136 build waves still had to fix this failure one recipe at
# a time (json_c, openal, libjxl, tweeny, and dozens more), despite #47 being in
# place. Measured on the #136 backlog: 79 of the 508 ports whose last outcome was
# a build-error carry the cmake-policy signature ("Compatibility with CMake < 3.5
# has been removed" / "add -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5"), and several of
# them (gflags, polyclipping, qhull, zopfli, uchardet) use an explicit arg list --
# so #47 could never have cleared them.
#
# THE SYSTEMIC FIX (#136, HaikuPorter/Utils.py:filteredEnvironment)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The header-environment claim above ("NOT a usable channel") was only half true:
# an export on the box is stripped, yes -- but the *reason* is filteredEnvironment(),
# and that is precisely where to set the default so it is NOT stripped. cmake >= 3.31
# reads CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM from the environment (applied before it parses
# any CMakeLists.txt), so a value present in the BUILD() shell's environment reaches
# EVERY cmake invocation regardless of how the recipe spells the command. haikuporter
# builds each port in a shell whose environment is exactly filteredEnvironment()'s
# return value. So seed the default there, alongside the LC_ALL/TERM defaults, and
# also pass an explicit os.environ override through so a recipe/operator can still win:
#
#   THE EDIT (HaikuPorter/Utils.py, filteredEnvironment):
#
#     	env = {
#     		'LC_ALL': 'POSIX',
#     		'TERM': 'xterm',
#   +		# graviton/DeBeOS (#136): default cmake's policy floor to 3.5 for
#   +		# EVERY cmake invocation in a port BUILD(), independent of how the
#   +		# recipe calls cmake. cmake >= 3.31 reads this from the environment,
#   +		# so it reaches recipes that pass an explicit arg list and never use
#   +		# $cmakeDirArgs. Only raises the floor; an explicit os.environ
#   +		# override still wins (passthrough loop below).
#   +		'CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM': '3.5',
#     	}
#
#   - 	for key in ['LIBRARY_PATH', 'PATH']:
#   + 	for key in ['LIBRARY_PATH', 'PATH', 'CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM']:
#     		if key in os.environ:
#     			env[key] = os.environ[key]
#
# VERIFIED on a real Graviton (c7g) builder, cmake 4.1.6:
#   * minimal reproducer, cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8): WITHOUT the env var
#     configure fails RC=1 with the removal signature; WITH CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_
#     MINIMUM=3.5 exported it configures RC=0. So cmake honours the env var.
#   * a sample of the #136 signature ports built RC=0 with NO per-recipe change,
#     including explicit-arg-list ports (#47's channel does not reach them).
#   * known-good CMake ports (re2, jsoncpp, pugixml) still build RC=0 -- the flag
#     only raises the floor, so projects declaring >= 3.5 are unaffected.
#
# Retire when: the builder's CMake is old enough to still honour <3.5 policies
# (it will not be) OR every in-tree CMake port declares a >=3.5 minimum. Until
# then this is a straight toolchain-compatibility default, not a feature cut.
